WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.588
Marilla had decided to keep Anne, but she didn't want to tell Anne until the next day.

2
00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:14.575
She took Anne upstairs and said, "Now, Anne, I noticed you threw all your clothes on the floor.

3
00:00:14.576 --> 00:00:19.790
That's a bad habit. Please fold your clothes and put them on the chair."

4
00:00:19.791 --> 00:00:26.429
"I was so upset last night I forgot," said Anne. "I'll fold them nicely tonight."

5
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.182
"Say your prayers and get into bed."

6
00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:32.950
"I never say any prayers," announced Anne.

7
00:00:32.951 --> 00:00:36.612
Marilla was horrified. "What do you mean?

8
00:00:36.613 --> 00:00:39.858
Were you never taught to say prayers?"

9
00:00:39.859 --> 00:00:44.882
"Well, Mrs. Thomas told me that God made my hair red on purpose.

10
00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:50.713
So I don't really care for God. Anyway, I'm always too tired to say prayers."

11
00:00:50.714 --> 00:00:55.293
"Well, you must say your prayers here," Marilla insisted.

12
00:00:55.294 --> 00:01:00.880
"Of course I will," said Anne cheerfully. "I'm ready. What do I say?"

13
00:01:00.881 --> 00:01:06.140
"Just thank God and ask for some things you want," Marilla told Anne.

14
00:01:06.141 --> 00:01:16.583
"I'll do my best," promised Anne. "Dear God, thank you for the wild cherry tree and the lake, which I call 'the Lake of Shining Waters.'

15
00:01:16.584 --> 00:01:20.653
I want so many things that it'll take a long time to say everything.

16
00:01:20.654 --> 00:01:29.358
So the most important things are these: please let me stay at Green Gables and please make me pretty when I grow up."

17
00:01:29.359 --> 00:01:34.342
Marilla waited until the next afternoon to tell Anne she could stay.

18
00:01:34.343 --> 00:01:40.542
During the morning Marilla asked Anne to do various tasks, and she watched Anne with a keen eye.

19
00:01:40.543 --> 00:01:47.736
By noon Marilla saw that Anne was a hard worker, quick to learn, clever, and obedient.

20
00:01:47.737 --> 00:01:56.329
Her most serious shortcoming was a tendency to start daydreaming in the middle of a task and forget everything until Marilla reprimanded her.

21
00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:00.526
When Anne finished washing dishes, she suddenly grabbed Marilla.

22
00:02:00.527 --> 00:02:05.189
"Oh please, Miss Cuthbert, can you tell me if I can stay or not?

23
00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:09.426
I've tried to be patient all morning. Please tell me."

24
00:02:09.427 --> 00:02:15.613
"You haven't rinsed the dishcloth in boiling water, Anne," said Marilla. "Do that first."

25
00:02:15.614 --> 00:02:20.353
Anne attended to the dishcloth and then looked at Marilla again.

26
00:02:20.354 --> 00:02:29.195
"Well," said Marilla, "Matthew and I decided to keep you— if you are a good girl. Anne, what's the matter?"

27
00:02:29.196 --> 00:02:38.299
"I'm crying," said Anne, "but I don't know why. I'm so happy. Oh, happy isn't the right word.

28
00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:44.765
I was happy to see the trees and flowers—but this! I'll try to be so good.

29
00:02:44.766 --> 00:02:52.419
Mrs. Thomas said I am wicked, so it will be difficult, but I'll try. But why am I crying, Marilla?"

30
00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:57.970
"I suppose because you're excited and worked up," said Marilla disapprovingly.

31
00:02:57.971 --> 00:03:04.127
"Sit down on that chair. Try to calm down. You laugh and cry far too easily.

32
00:03:04.128 --> 00:03:10.678
Now, you must go to school when it starts in September. Until then you can help me here."

33
00:03:10.679 --> 00:03:15.067
"What will I call you? Miss Cuthbert? Aunt Marilla?"

34
00:03:15.068 --> 00:03:22.106
"No, just Marilla. I'm not used to Miss Cuthbert. Just plain Marilla is fine."

35
00:03:22.107 --> 00:03:27.390
"It sounds awfully disrespectful to say just Marilla," protested Anne.

36
00:03:27.391 --> 00:03:33.936
"Everybody else does. Make sure you speak politely, and it will be fine," Marilla replied.

37
00:03:33.937 --> 00:03:38.292
"I'd love to call you Aunt Marilla," said Anne.

38
00:03:38.293 --> 00:03:45.097
"I've never had an aunt or any relation at all, not even a grandmother. Please?"

39
00:03:45.098 --> 00:03:50.681
"No, you can't. I don't believe in calling people names that don't belong to them."

40
00:03:50.682 --> 00:03:53.154
"But we could imagine you're my aunt."

41
00:03:53.155 --> 00:03:56.204
"I couldn't," said Marilla grimly.

42
00:03:56.205 --> 00:04:02.406
"Do you ever imagine things different from what they really are, Marilla?" asked Anne, wide-eyed.

43
00:04:02.407 --> 00:04:04.960
"No," said Marilla.

44
00:04:04.961 --> 00:04:13.892
"Oh!" Anne drew a long breath. Then she spoke. "Oh, Marilla, how much you miss!"

45
00:04:13.893 --> 00:04:20.736
Later Anne asked, "Marilla, do you think I will ever have a kindred spirit in Avonlea?"

46
00:04:20.737 --> 00:04:23.985
"A . . . a what?" asked Marilla.

47
00:04:23.986 --> 00:04:30.605
"A kindred spirit, a best friend in whom I can confide my innermost soul.

48
00:04:30.606 --> 00:04:33.415
I've dreamed of meeting her all my life.

49
00:04:33.416 --> 00:04:43.586
I never really supposed I would, but so many of my dreams have come true all at once that perhaps this one will too. Do you think it's possible?"

50
00:04:43.587 --> 00:04:48.848
"Diana Barry lives nearby, and she's about your age," Marilla replied.

51
00:04:48.849 --> 00:04:55.062
"She's a very nice girl, and perhaps she can be your playmate when she comes home.

52
00:04:55.063 --> 00:05:00.082
She's visiting her aunt now. You'll have to be careful how you behave though.

53
00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:08.096
Mrs. Barry is very particular. She won't let Diana play with any girl who isn't nice and good."

54
00:05:08.097 --> 00:05:15.542
"What is Diana like?" Anne asked. "Her hair isn't red, is it? Oh, I hope not.

55
00:05:15.543 --> 00:05:22.879
It's bad enough to have red hair myself, but I positively couldn't endure it in a best friend too."

56
00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:26.635
"Diana is a very pretty girl," said Marilla.

57
00:05:26.636 --> 00:05:30.162
"She has black eyes and hair and rosy cheeks.

58
00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:35.508
And she is good and smart, which is better than being pretty."

59
00:05:35.509 --> 00:05:39.101
"I'm so glad she's pretty," Anne said.

60
00:05:39.102 --> 00:05:43.780
"I'm not beautiful, so having a beautiful friend would be wonderful.

61
00:05:43.781 --> 00:05:48.518
When I lived with Mrs. Thomas, there was a bookcase with glass doors.

62
00:05:48.519 --> 00:05:55.578
One of the doors was broken because Mr. Thomas smashed it when he was drunk. The other glass door was whole.

63
00:05:55.579 --> 00:06:00.971
I used to pretend that my reflection was another little girl who lived in the glass.

64
00:06:00.972 --> 00:06:06.366
"Her name was Katie, and we were very close. I told her everything.

65
00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:11.845
Katie was my only friend. We pretended that the bookcase was enchanted.

66
00:06:11.846 --> 00:06:14.912
I knew the spell that took me to Katie's world.

67
00:06:14.913 --> 00:06:22.174
In Katie's world there were flowers and fairies and sunshine, and we would live there happily ever after.

68
00:06:22.175 --> 00:06:29.436
When I went to live with Mrs. Hammond, I was so upset to leave Katie. She was sad too."

69
00:06:29.437 --> 00:06:33.563
Marilla listened and then gave Anne a strange look.

70
00:06:33.564 --> 00:06:35.859
"I don't approve of such things, Anne.

71
00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:39.046
You seem to half-believe your own imagination.

72
00:06:39.047 --> 00:06:44.653
Don't let Mrs. Barry hear you talking about your friend Katie. She'll think you're strange."

73
00:06:44.654 --> 00:06:51.316
"Oh, I won't," said Anne. "I won't tell anybody. But I thought you'd like to know."

74
00:06:51.317 --> 00:06:57.055
"Well," Marilla said, smiling. "You'll have a real friend soon, Anne."

75
00:06:57.056 --> 00:07:01.640
"Look, there's a big bee in that apple blossom!" said Anne.

76
00:07:01.641 --> 00:07:07.022
"If I wasn't human, I think I'd like to be a bee and live in the flowers!"

77
00:07:07.023 --> 00:07:10.953
"Yesterday you wanted to be a bird," said Marilla.

78
00:07:10.954 --> 00:07:15.924
"You are very fickle. Now just be quiet for a minute!

79
00:07:15.925 --> 00:07:24.520
It seems impossible for you to stop talking if you've got anybody who will listen to you!"

